#: src/ai/external-agents.md:38 src/ai/external-agents.md:92
#: src/ai/external-agents.md:175
msgid "Installation"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:40
msgid ""
"The first time you create a Gemini CLI thread, Zed will install [@google/"
"gemini-cli](https://github.com/google-gemini/gemini-cli). This installation "
"is only available to Zed and is kept up to date as you use the agent."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:43 src/ai/external-agents.md:84
#: src/ai/external-agents.md:159 src/ai/external-agents.md:290
msgid "Authentication"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:45
msgid "After you have Gemini CLI running, you'll be prompted to authenticate."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:47
msgid ""
"Click the \"Login\" button to open the Gemini CLI interactively, where you "
"can log in with your Google account or [Vertex AI](https://cloud.google.com/"
"vertex-ai) credentials. Zed does not see your OAuth or access tokens in this "
"case."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:50
msgid ""
"If the `GEMINI_API_KEY` environment variable (or `GOOGLE_AI_API_KEY`) is "
"already set, or you have configured a Google AI API key in Zed's [language "
"model provider settings](./llm-providers.md#google-ai), it will be passed to "
"Gemini CLI automatically."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:52
msgid ""
"For more information, see the [Gemini CLI docs](https://github.com/google-"
"gemini/gemini-cli/blob/main/docs/index.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:54 src/ai/external-agents.md:114
#: src/ai/external-agents.md:182
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:56
msgid ""
"Gemini CLI supports the same workflows as Zed's first-party agent: code "
"generation, refactoring, debugging, and Q&A. Add context by @-mentioning "
"files, recent threads, or symbols."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:58
msgid ""
"Some agent panel features are not yet available with Gemini CLI: editing "
"past messages, resuming threads from history, and checkpointing."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:60 src/ai/external-agents.md:279
msgid "Claude Agent"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:62
msgid ""
"Similar to Gemini CLI, you can also run [Claude Agent](https://platform."
"claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/overview) directly via Zed's [agent panel](./"
"agent-panel.md). Under the hood, Zed runs the Claude Agent SDK, which runs "
"Claude Code under the hood, and communicates to it over ACP, through [a "
"dedicated adapter](https://github.com/zed-industries/claude-agent-acp)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:67
msgid ""
"Open the agent panel with <kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-?\\|ctrl-?</kbd>, "
"and then use the `+` button in the top right to start a new Claude Agent "
"thread."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:75 src/ai/external-agents.md:150
msgid "\"cmd-alt-c\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:77 src/ai/external-agents.md:104
msgid "\"claude-acp\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:86
msgid ""
"As of version `0.202.7`, authentication to Zed's Claude Agent installation "
"is decoupled entirely from Zed's agent. That is to say, an Anthropic API key "
"added via the [Zed Agent's settings](./llm-providers.md#anthropic) will "
"_not_ be utilized by Claude Agent for authentication and billing."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:89
msgid ""
"To ensure you're using your billing method of choice, [open a new Claude "
"Agent thread](./agent-panel.md#new-thread). Then, run `/login`, and "
"authenticate either via API key, or via `Log in with Claude Code` to use a "
"Claude Pro/Max subscription."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:94
msgid ""
"The first time you create a Claude Agent thread, Zed will install [@zed-"
"industries/claude-agent-acp](https://github.com/zed-industries/claude-agent-"
"acp). This installation is only available to Zed and is kept up to date as "
"you use the agent."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:97
msgid ""
"Zed will always use this managed version of the Claude Agent adapter, which "
"includes a vendored version of the Claude Code CLI, even if you have it "
"installed globally."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:99
msgid ""
"If you want to override the executable used by the adapter, you can set the "
"`CLAUDE_CODE_EXECUTABLE` environment variable in your settings to the path "
"of your preferred executable."
msgstr ""

