#: src/ai/external-agents.md:116
msgid ""
"Claude Agent supports the same workflows as Zed's first-party agent. Add "
"context by @-mentioning files, recent threads, diagnostics, or symbols."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:118
msgid ""
"In complement to talking to it [over ACP](https://agentclientprotocol.com), "
"Zed relies on the [Claude Agent SDK](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/"
"agent-sdk/overview) to support some of its specific features. However, the "
"SDK doesn't yet expose everything needed to fully support all of them:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:121
msgid ""
"Slash Commands: [Custom slash commands](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/"
"slash-commands#custom-slash-commands) are fully supported, and have been "
"merged into skills. A subset of [built-in commands](https://code.claude.com/"
"docs/en/slash-commands#built-in-slash-commands) are supported."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:122
msgid "[Subagents](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/sub-agents) are supported."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:123
msgid ""
"[Agent teams](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-teams) are currently "
"_not_ supported."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:124
msgid ""
"[Hooks](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks-guide) are currently _not_ "
"supported."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:126
msgid ""
"Some [agent panel](./agent-panel.md) features are not yet available with "
"Claude Agent: editing past messages, resuming threads from history, and "
"checkpointing."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:128
msgid "CLAUDE.md"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:130
msgid ""
"Claude Agent in Zed will automatically use any `CLAUDE.md` file found in "
"your project root, project subdirectories, or root `.claude` directory."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:132
msgid ""
"If you don't have a `CLAUDE.md` file, you can ask Claude Agent to create one "
"for you through the `init` slash command."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:134
msgid "Codex CLI"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:136
msgid ""
"You can also run [Codex CLI](https://github.com/openai/codex) directly via "
"Zed's [agent panel](./agent-panel.md). Under the hood, Zed runs Codex CLI "
"and communicates to it over ACP, through [a dedicated adapter](https://"
"github.com/zed-industries/codex-acp)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:141
msgid ""
"As of version `0.208`, you should be able to use Codex directly from Zed. "
"Open the agent panel with <kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-?\\|ctrl-?</kbd>, "
"and then use the `+` button in the top right to start a new Codex thread."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:152 src/ai/external-agents.md:311
msgid "\"codex-acp\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:161
msgid ""
"Authentication to Zed's Codex installation is decoupled entirely from Zed's "
"agent. That is to say, an OpenAI API key added via the [Zed Agent's settings]"
"(./llm-providers.md#openai) will _not_ be utilized by Codex for "
"authentication and billing."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:164
msgid ""
"To ensure you're using your billing method of choice, [open a new Codex "
"thread](./agent-panel.md#new-thread). The first time you will be prompted to "
"authenticate with one of three methods:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:167
msgid ""
"Login with ChatGPT - allows you to use your existing, paid ChatGPT "
"subscription. _Note: This method isn't currently supported in remote "
"projects_"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:168
msgid ""
"`CODEX_API_KEY` - uses an API key you have set in your environment under the "
"variable `CODEX_API_KEY`."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:169
msgid ""
"`OPENAI_API_KEY` - uses an API key you have set in your environment under "
"the variable `OPENAI_API_KEY`."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:171
msgid ""
"If you are already logged in and want to change your authentication method, "
"type `/logout` in the thread and authenticate again."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:173
msgid ""
"If you want to use a third-party provider with Codex, you can configure that "
"with your [Codex config.toml](https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/main/docs/"
"config.md#model-selection) or pass extra [args/env variables](https://github."
"com/openai/codex/blob/main/docs/config.md#model-selection) to your Codex "
"agent servers settings."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:177
msgid ""
"The first time you create a Codex thread, Zed will install [codex-acp]"
"(https://github.com/zed-industries/codex-acp). This installation is only "
"available to Zed and is kept up to date as you use the agent."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:180
msgid ""
"Zed will always use this managed version of Codex even if you have it "
"installed globally."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:184
msgid ""
"Codex supports the same workflows as Zed's first-party agent. Add context by "
"@-mentioning files or symbols."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:186
msgid ""
"Some agent panel features are not yet available with Codex: editing past "
"messages, resuming threads from history, and checkpointing."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:188
msgid "Add More Agents"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:190
msgid "Via Agent Server Extensions"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:194
msgid ""
"Starting from `v0.221.x`, [the ACP Registry](https://agentclientprotocol.com/"
"registry) is the preferred way to install external agents in Zed. Learn more "
"about it in [the release blog post](https://zed.dev/blog/acp-registry). At "
"some point in the near future, Agent Server extensions will be deprecated."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:200
msgid ""
"Add more external agents to Zed by installing [Agent Server extensions](../"
"extensions/agent-servers.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:202
msgid ""
"See what agents are available by filtering for \"Agent Servers\" in the "
"extensions page, which you can access via the command palette with `zed: "
"extensions`, or the [Zed website](https://zed.dev/extensions?filter=agent-"
"servers)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:204
msgid "Via The ACP Registry"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:206
msgid "Overview"
msgstr "概覽"

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:208
msgid ""
"As mentioned above, the Agent Server extensions will be deprecated in the "
"near future to give room to the ACP Registry."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:210
msgid ""
"[The ACP Registry](https://github.com/agentclientprotocol/registry) lets "
"developers distribute ACP-compatible agents to any client that implements "
"the protocol. Agents installed from the registry update automatically."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:212
msgid ""
"At the moment, the registry is a curated set of agents, including only the "
"ones that [support authentication](https://agentclientprotocol.com/rfds/auth-"
"methods)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:214
msgid "Using it in Zed"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:216
msgid ""
"Use the `zed: acp registry` command to quickly go to the ACP Registry page. "
"There's also a button (\"Add Agent\") that takes you there in the agent "
"panel's configuration view."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:219
msgid ""
"From there, you can click to install your preferred agent and it will become "
"available right away in the `+` icon button in the agent panel."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:221
msgid ""
"If you installed the same agent through both the extension and the registry, "
"the registry version takes precedence."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:223
msgid "Custom Agents"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:225
msgid ""
"You can also add agents through your settings file ([how to edit](../"
"configuring-zed.md#settings-files)) by specifying certain fields under "
"`agent_servers`, like so:"
msgstr ""

