msgid "\"--acp\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:240
msgid ""
"This can be useful if you're in the middle of developing a new agent that "
"speaks the protocol and you want to debug it."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:242
msgid ""
"It's also possible to customize environment variables for registry-installed "
"agents like Claude Agent, Codex, and Gemini CLI by using their registry "
"names (`claude-acp`, `codex-acp`, `gemini`) with `\"type\": \"registry\"` in "
"your settings."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:244
msgid "Debugging Agents"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:246
msgid ""
"When using external agents in Zed, you can access the debug view via with "
"`dev: open acp logs` from the Command Palette. This lets you see the "
"messages being sent and received between Zed and the agent."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:249
msgid "![The debug view for ACP logs.](https://zed.dev/img/acp/acp-logs.webp)"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:251
msgid ""
"It's helpful to attach data from this view if you're opening issues about "
"problems with external agents like Claude Agent, Codex, OpenCode, etc."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:253
msgid "Configuration Boundaries"
msgstr ""

